        "rationale": "Both resynchronization paths are now retained and both satisfy their obligations. Append-path branch: the restarted member reported leader 1 and applied the entry committed while it was down (indices 37: commit and applied index 3, payload on all three nodes), then proposed successfully (indices 38, 39). Snapshot branch: the leader snapshotted at index 3 (term 1) and compacted to 3 (index 41), the rebuilt member installed the snapshot with applied and commit index 3 while reporting leader 1 (index 42: installed true), and a proposal made afterwards returned with no error and was applied by node 2 with its payload on all three nodes (indices 43, 44). The two branches together cover the recovery mechanism the axes call out: a member that fell behind is restored either from the log tail or from a snapshot, and in both cases it returns to participating in decisions. No defect is claimed; the recovery obligation was met in both branches in this scenario.",
