        "joint_history": "The two receipts branch from the same prefix in the same harness and cluster: both build configuration {1,2,3} from the same storage ConfState, elect leader 1, commit a payload on all nodes, stop node 2 and commit a second payload with nodes 1 and 3. They diverge at resynchronization: receipt 2cd3883705a64c35aa04ba14b815ea42 restarts node 2 immediately so it catches up through the append path, while receipt fb60c74855614813a5c37afdae0bd4f9 first creates a snapshot on the leader at its last index and compacts the log to that index, so the missing entries are unavailable and node 2 must install the snapshot. Identity, membership and the pre-divergence history are therefore shared, and the cited indices belong to their own branch: the append branch's apply/commit indices are 36, 37 and its proposal results 38, 39; the snapshot branch's events are 41 to 44.",
